{
  "_fixture_note": [
    "A hand-written recon map, shaped like a real one but small enough to reason about.",
    "It is hand-written rather than a copied real run for two reasons. A real run is 400KB of",
    "screens nobody can hold in their head, so a test that fails against it tells you a number",
    "moved and not which rule broke. And a real run does not reliably contain the shapes worth",
    "testing - a real pass may happen to have no sinks and no contradictory crops at all.",
    "",
    "Every shape the builder has a branch for is present here on purpose:",
    "  sc01  the start screen: elements with measured boxes, one placed from a description",
    "        alone, a vetting refusal, and an inert input that changed nothing",
    "  sc02  reached and left again, and a variant transition whose crops are byte-identical",
    "        while it reports 14 cells changed - the frames-vs-counts finding",
    "  sc03  identity_is_weak, so every claim about it inherits that doubt",
    "  sc04  a SINK: entered from sc01 and never left",
    "  sc05  never entered, never left, unreachable from the start - the honest limit of a map",
    "",
    "The crop files are not committed. The test writes them, which is what makes the",
    "byte-identical pair an explicit fact of the test rather than an accident of what got",
    "checked in; with no crops on disk the builder reports 0 pairs checked and still builds."
  ],
